<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jezzar Pasha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1720–1804</span> · Also known as Ahmad Pasha al-Jazzar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jezzar Pasha, Ahmad Pasha al-Jazzar, was an Ottoman governor of Bosnian origin who ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a> as governor of Sidon from 1775 until his death in 1804. Known as &quot;the Butcher&quot; for his cruelty, he built up Acre's fortifications, mosque and markets and dominated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a>. With British naval help he held Acre against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s siege in 1799.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jezzar-pasha.jpg" alt="Jezzar Pasha" width="320" height="329" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Aldridge · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jezzar_Pasha,_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
